1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,720
[Disclaimer:
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,480
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:17,360
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:30,460
I heard from the main house
that you're back.

5
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:32,450
At first, it was quite hard to believe.

6
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:35,840
There's no place like home, right?

7
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:38,080
Even Ko Pha-ngan can't beat it.

8
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,710
There's a lot to catch up on.

9
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,040
Mr. Sarm...

10
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:49,470
Wait.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,000
What about us?

12
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,050
What is it?

13
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,000
Let go.

14
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,040
I am going home.

15
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:55,850
But you're my spouse.

16
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:57,050
Someone like you

17
00:00:57,190 --> 00:00:59,400
could only be my last choice.

18
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,650
Because...

19
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:01,670
you are not

20
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:02,250
hot!

21
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:07,400
Attention, attention.

22
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:11,180
The annual marathon is about to begin.

23
00:01:11,330 --> 00:01:14,330
In the lead, it's Jiranat,

24
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:15,250
nat, nat, nat...

25
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:16,860
He's a runner from Bangkok

26
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:20,039
who's No. 1 when it comes to running...

27
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:21,060
Why is that?!

28
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:23,690
Because he's the only person running...

29
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:26,460
He's even won a 4x100m relay,

30
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:29,010
with countless trophies to boot.

31
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:30,010
But why

32
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:30,810
doesn't he

33
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:32,970
stop running?!

34
00:01:33,450 --> 00:01:35,090
This is your final warning.

35
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:36,620
Will you stop running the easy way

36
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:41,250
or the hard way, way, way?

37
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:16,860
The ghosts here

38
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:18,890
are really fierce, you know?

39
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:21,840
They kidnap

40
00:02:22,329 --> 00:02:23,520
children and eat them alive!

41
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,540
Anyone who likes
playing hide-and-seek at night

42
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:29,829
is gonna get it.

43
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,079
No one is as much of a ghost as you!

44
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:41,440
Hey...

45
00:02:41,810 --> 00:02:42,530
Jam.

46
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:43,530
Jam!

47
00:02:44,410 --> 00:02:44,920
Jam!!

48
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:46,260
Jam!

49
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:46,960
Little Jam!

50
00:02:47,050 --> 00:02:48,050
Little Jam, I'm so sorry!

51
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:48,960
Little Jam!

52
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,250
Little Jam!

53
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,260
I'm sorry.

54
00:02:52,010 --> 00:02:53,010
Little Jam...

55
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,160
From the looks of it,

56
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,740
I guess I'll be his Pak Chong
branch spouse for quite a while.

57
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:31,460
[Your Third Series]

58
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:45,690
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

59
00:04:45,730 --> 00:04:50,170
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

60
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:54,830
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

61
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:59,590
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

62
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:04,570
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

63
00:05:04,590 --> 00:05:09,030
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

64
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:13,420
♫But when they make you blue,♫

65
00:05:13,470 --> 00:05:17,180
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

66
00:05:18,150 --> 00:05:22,820
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

67
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:26,610
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

68
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:31,630
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

69
00:05:31,710 --> 00:05:36,180
♫At least being your third still counts♫

70
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:41,130
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

71
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:44,840
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

72
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:49,980
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

73
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,990
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

74
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:55,220
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

75
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,730
[Your Third Series]

76
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:27,370
"The laundry is hanging in the closet.

77
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,170
Your backpack is on the sofa.

78
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:33,750
Take care of everything yourself,

79
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:37,440
and have breakfast downstairs,

80
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:38,870
please.

81
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:40,670
From...

82
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:44,170
your Pak Chong branch spouse."

83
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:50,080
You crazy Mr. Sarm.

84
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:52,770
You are annoying as hell.

85
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:08,690
Mr. Jam, you're awake?

86
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,540
Would you like some breakfast?

87
00:07:10,710 --> 00:07:12,650
For breakfast, we have
fried rice with crab, crab stew,

88
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:14,550
and steamed egg with crab meat.

89
00:07:16,410 --> 00:07:17,810
Or, if you'd like anything else,

90
00:07:17,830 --> 00:07:18,980
just let me know.

91
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:23,050
In that case...

92
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,510
I will have the fried rice with crab.

93
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:26,900
Certainly, Mr. Jam.

94
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,320
Sorry to trouble you,

95
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:29,680
but I am starving.

96
00:07:30,130 --> 00:07:31,510
Please have a seat, Mr. Jam.

97
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:32,940
Right. Thank you.

98
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:47,120
Please wait a moment.

99
00:07:47,230 --> 00:07:48,020
Sure.

100
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,440
Here you go,

101
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,750
your fried rice with crab.

102
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,210
Here.

103
00:08:06,230 --> 00:08:07,740
It looks delicious.

104
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:09,600
Please, eat up.

105
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:10,510
Right.

106
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:16,850
Thank you very much.

107
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:18,670
It tastes wonderful.

108
00:08:18,690 --> 00:08:19,390
Right.

109
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:20,410
Please, eat up.

110
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,120
Auntie.

111
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:36,429
Where is Mr. Sarm?

112
00:08:37,049 --> 00:08:38,720
He's been gone since early this morning.

113
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:40,340
He didn't say where he was going.

114
00:08:40,549 --> 00:08:41,929
He only told me

115
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:44,350
to prepare breakfast for you.

116
00:08:47,490 --> 00:08:50,030
If I want to meet Mr. Sarm,

117
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:51,720
where do I have to go?

118
00:08:52,330 --> 00:08:53,130
Today,

119
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:55,220
I intend to clear things up with him.

120
00:09:07,830 --> 00:09:08,830
I'm always here.

121
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:11,140
I'll take my leave now.

122
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,530
What is it, hmm?

123
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:22,940
What is it you want to talk about?

124
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:26,240
I want to talk to you

125
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:29,200
about that night.

126
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:42,000
That night...

127
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:46,330
Which one?

128
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,830
Well, that one.

129
00:09:59,130 --> 00:09:59,920
Which one?

130
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,320
My God...

131
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:05,010
We are already off to a confusing start?

132
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:07,030
That night.

133
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:09,040
Oh.

134
00:10:09,430 --> 00:10:10,660
That full-moon night?

135
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,140
That night.

136
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:13,340
That one!

137
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:13,870
Oh.

138
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,840
That starlit night?

139
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:17,910
Gosh... Mr. Sarm.

140
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:19,510
Why would I know which night it is?

141
00:10:19,830 --> 00:10:21,020
We were together every night.

142
00:10:21,970 --> 00:10:22,760
That night.

143
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:23,950
Which night is it, Little Jam?

144
00:10:24,350 --> 00:10:26,430
The night you and I...

145
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:38,350
Well, it already happened,

146
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:43,230
but you do not have to act like
we are actually something.

147
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:46,920
Because, in truth, we are not.

148
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:50,870
I do not think of you in that light either.

149
00:10:51,930 --> 00:10:53,240
Your words.

150
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:54,430
Aren't you a feisty one?

151
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:56,350
You're so talented

152
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:57,740
and wonderful.

153
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,220
You just live your life,

154
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,710
and I will go back to living mine.

155
00:11:07,030 --> 00:11:07,630
Jam...

156
00:11:08,450 --> 00:11:09,630
you think it's that simple?

157
00:11:09,650 --> 00:11:11,820
And why complicate things at all?

158
00:11:14,470 --> 00:11:16,220
You might have just been lonely back then,

159
00:11:24,330 --> 00:11:26,870
and I just happened to be there.

160
00:11:33,830 --> 00:11:34,920
This is going way too far, Jam.

161
00:11:39,770 --> 00:11:40,680
Mr. Sib!

162
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,310
I have to go now.

163
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:44,130
Jam.

164
00:11:44,830 --> 00:11:45,440
Hold on.

165
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:47,030
We're not done here.

166
00:11:47,430 --> 00:11:48,110
Little Jam.

167
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:50,020
Yes, Mr. Sib?

168
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:53,620
Gosh, Sib!

169
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:55,790
You're calling him at the worst time.

170
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,350
Mr. Sib.

171
00:12:45,350 --> 00:12:46,230
Oh, Jam.

172
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,240
How are you?

173
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,130
Did you sleep well last night?

174
00:12:50,690 --> 00:12:51,360
Well...

175
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:53,630
I did.

176
00:12:54,370 --> 00:12:55,140
If so,

177
00:12:55,190 --> 00:12:57,240
please tell me what happened on Ko Pha-ngan.

178
00:13:01,130 --> 00:13:03,020
Mr. Sarm. He...

179
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,130
By the way,

180
00:13:05,150 --> 00:13:06,460
have you really thought this through?

181
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:08,820
About limiting the number of visitors?

182
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:10,830
I don't think it'll work.

183
00:13:11,030 --> 00:13:11,860
The reason?

184
00:13:13,330 --> 00:13:14,620
Adisuan Farm stretches far and wide,

185
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,930
spanning three districts.

186
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:18,640
So why limit the number of visitors?

187
00:13:19,190 --> 00:13:21,220
Uncle Decha managed it just fine
back in his day,

188
00:13:21,330 --> 00:13:22,870
when tourists were packed
shoulder to shoulder.

189
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:25,730
Instead of making the most of it,

190
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,120
you just threw away the opportunity.

191
00:13:30,370 --> 00:13:31,620
Past success

192
00:13:32,330 --> 00:13:34,160
doesn't guarantee success today.

193
00:13:36,070 --> 00:13:37,240
I still stand by what I said:

194
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:39,430
Adisuan Farm

195
00:13:40,170 --> 00:13:41,630
doesn't need to maximize profits;

196
00:13:42,230 --> 00:13:43,640
it needs to be as stable as possible.

197
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:46,030
There was one night
when those guys followed us

198
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,040
and found both of us.

199
00:13:48,530 --> 00:13:51,150
They took Mr. Sarm and me onto a boat.

200
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:53,410
Then they threw me into the sea.

201
00:13:54,170 --> 00:13:57,430
I have no idea
what happened to Mr. Sarm that night,

202
00:13:58,220 --> 00:13:59,940
but he looked rather down.

203
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,670
Then, a few nights later,

204
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:06,070
he said a wild bull was after him.

205
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:08,040
A wild bull?

206
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:14,960
Mr. Sarm, he...

207
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:18,720
Who has he been having problems with?

208
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:21,030
If it's about his work,

209
00:14:21,430 --> 00:14:23,640
I don't really know
whose toes he might have stepped on.

210
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:25,100
But he's

211
00:14:25,130 --> 00:14:27,640
the type who would break rather than bend.

212
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:30,240
He'd meet up with anyone
who had a problem with him

213
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:32,730
and settle the score then and there.

214
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:35,740
But judging from everything,

215
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:37,010
I believe...

216
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:40,540
it's more of an internal conflict.

217
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:42,130
And there's only one suspect.

218
00:14:43,330 --> 00:14:45,090
Mr. Sib, are you saying that...

219
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:46,820
While you were away,

220
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:49,130
your brother Sib

221
00:14:49,150 --> 00:14:50,510
caused no end of trouble.

222
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,220
Last time,

223
00:14:52,310 --> 00:14:54,230
he sent someone to audit the accounts.

224
00:14:55,210 --> 00:14:56,210
Today,

225
00:14:57,430 --> 00:14:59,240
he sent someone to inspect our system here.

226
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:01,130
Don't you think that's odd?

227
00:15:02,330 --> 00:15:03,550
I'm fairly certain who it is,

228
00:15:04,110 --> 00:15:06,820
but making accusations without proof

229
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:08,130
won't do us any good.

230
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:10,240
We need some evidence first.

231
00:15:12,230 --> 00:15:13,330
This is Thee,

232
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:15,910
my dad's nephew.

233
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:17,580
Thee started working at Adisuan Farm

234
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,680
when Sarm returned to Thailand.

235
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,790
Back then,
Adisuan Farm was about to collapse,

236
00:15:22,810 --> 00:15:24,610
but the two of them fought through it all

237
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,920
and brought this place this far.

238
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:29,520
They had been through so much together

239
00:15:30,350 --> 00:15:31,630
and had even been very close once.

240
00:15:31,910 --> 00:15:34,530
Why do you suspect Mr. Thee?

241
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:35,950
The tide is out,

242
00:15:36,290 --> 00:15:37,130
so the truth is surfacing.

243
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:39,820
I once told Sib

244
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:41,920
that if something happened to me,

245
00:15:42,870 --> 00:15:44,240
he'd take the helm in my place.

246
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:48,740
I'm just an outsider, huh?

247
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:50,540
Why are you saying that?

248
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,340
You're still a brother to me.

249
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:59,130
Who did he send here, anyway?

250
00:16:00,350 --> 00:16:01,430
I have no idea about that.

251
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:04,590
And that's what I want to talk to you about.

252
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,040
I'm not going to beat around the bush.

253
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:09,630
I want you to gather
solid evidence against Mr. Thee

254
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:13,220
while learning how everything works here

255
00:16:13,470 --> 00:16:15,310
within three months.

256
00:16:19,370 --> 00:16:20,120
But...

257
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,230
I'm not forcing you
to take on this assignment.

258
00:16:22,590 --> 00:16:24,250
That's why I wanted your two cents first.

259
00:16:24,930 --> 00:16:25,840
What do you think?

260
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,630
I was wondering, with a deal this big,

261
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:32,870
why do you not talk to Mr. Sarm about it?

262
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:34,920
I'd rather not.

263
00:16:35,390 --> 00:16:37,020
All he does is get on my nerves.

264
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:38,920
I can't be bothered talking to him.

265
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,120
But honestly,

266
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,020
I can just stay out of this.

267
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:45,930
Sarm can take care of himself,

268
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,230
but problems will drag on and on

269
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:49,160
with something

270
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:52,050
like a wild bull, a tiger,
or whatever he calls it.

271
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:57,320
Sib walked his own path.

272
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:59,130
The same goes for Namnueng

273
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:01,590
and Song.

274
00:17:02,530 --> 00:17:04,020
Our parents went their own way, too.

275
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:06,930
That's why
I don't want to be with my family.

276
00:17:08,329 --> 00:17:09,740
But what's important is that

277
00:17:10,130 --> 00:17:10,930
this matter

278
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:12,730
involves someone close to him,

279
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:15,849
so emotions are definitely running high,

280
00:17:16,250 --> 00:17:17,520
since the two of them grew up together.

281
00:17:18,329 --> 00:17:20,849
I'm not sure how he'll take it

282
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:22,819
