417
00:23:00,450 --> 00:23:02,430
Mr. Sib is actually not a strict man.

418
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,540
Once you figure him out,

419
00:23:04,740 --> 00:23:06,830
you will see that he is very kind-hearted.

420
00:23:07,030 --> 00:23:07,880
Well then...

421
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:10,210
I guess you will have to
figure Mr. Sarm out

422
00:23:10,230 --> 00:23:11,750
so that things go smoothly for you.

423
00:23:15,450 --> 00:23:17,140
Figuring him out is difficult,

424
00:23:17,330 --> 00:23:19,620
but sealing his soul into a pot
and sinking it

425
00:23:19,670 --> 00:23:20,740
is certainly not!

426
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:25,220
Wasin!

427
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:27,820
Wasin, wait for me, please!

428
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:44,510
Little Jam.

429
00:23:50,860 --> 00:23:52,520
I just drove past Mr. Wasin,

430
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:53,640
so I knew you were here.

431
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:56,330
Where are you off to?

432
00:23:57,740 --> 00:23:59,340
What business do you have with me?

433
00:24:03,060 --> 00:24:04,110
I wish I do, actually.

434
00:24:06,930 --> 00:24:08,320
Mr. Sarm, do you see...

435
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:10,740
that spot?

436
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:21,250
Is that where our future lies?

437
00:24:22,590 --> 00:24:24,330
I am just saying, you can go

438
00:24:24,350 --> 00:24:26,440
joke around over there

439
00:24:27,410 --> 00:24:28,740
by yourself.

440
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:32,430
But you still haven't told me

441
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:33,630
where you're going.

442
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:35,670
I am going to get some stuff from my house.

443
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:36,940
Let's go, then.

444
00:24:40,250 --> 00:24:41,020
Wait.

445
00:24:41,650 --> 00:24:43,750
I did not tell you to join me.

446
00:24:51,450 --> 00:24:52,530
Please, Little Jam.

447
00:24:54,390 --> 00:24:55,240
Come with me.

448
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:56,670
Leave your car here

449
00:24:56,840 --> 00:24:57,840
and go there with me.

450
00:24:58,130 --> 00:24:59,640
I have something important
to talk to you about.

451
00:25:08,300 --> 00:25:09,300
Pin the location for me.

452
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:24,440
How's work today?

453
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:25,550
Pretty good.

454
00:25:25,830 --> 00:25:26,830
Do you like it here?

455
00:25:30,580 --> 00:25:31,180
I do.

456
00:25:32,340 --> 00:25:33,640
The weather here is lovely.

457
00:25:34,830 --> 00:25:36,140
And...

458
00:25:36,570 --> 00:25:37,740
how is it

459
00:25:37,760 --> 00:25:38,940
working with Mr. Wasin?

460
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:40,360
He is kind.

461
00:25:40,910 --> 00:25:43,460
He treated me to a cup of bubble tea
in the afternoon, too.

462
00:25:44,770 --> 00:25:45,830
Can I borrow your phone?

463
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:57,030
[Contact: Your Sarm]

464
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:01,510
You are not mine.

465
00:26:02,130 --> 00:26:03,510
Then what cat would I belong to,
if not you?

466
00:26:03,530 --> 00:26:04,280
Whether it's rain,

467
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:05,060
a downpour,

468
00:26:05,090 --> 00:26:05,720
no running water,

469
00:26:05,740 --> 00:26:06,280
a power outage,

470
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:06,910
or you just miss me,

471
00:26:06,930 --> 00:26:07,580
need a hug,

472
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:09,440
or want to be clingy with me,

473
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:10,740
I'm always just one call away.

474
00:26:11,450 --> 00:26:13,060
Though I'm not an authority,

475
00:26:13,580 --> 00:26:14,360
I am a

476
00:26:14,390 --> 00:26:15,120
M.W.

477
00:26:15,150 --> 00:26:16,150
H.C.

478
00:26:16,170 --> 00:26:17,130
O.Y.

479
00:26:17,150 --> 00:26:22,550
[M.W.H.C.O.Y]

480
00:26:24,420 --> 00:26:25,520
What does that stand for?

481
00:26:27,060 --> 00:26:28,630
Call me by my name first

482
00:26:28,650 --> 00:26:29,390
and I'll tell you.

483
00:26:30,740 --> 00:26:32,140
I do not want to know either way.

484
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:34,010
"A Man Who Has a Crush On You."

485
00:26:36,860 --> 00:26:37,500
Little Jam!

486
00:26:38,610 --> 00:26:40,070
Can you not honk the horn like that?

487
00:26:40,860 --> 00:26:41,610
I told you...

488
00:26:43,460 --> 00:26:44,120
Stop, stop, stop.

489
00:26:47,310 --> 00:26:48,600
Little Jam, don't!

490
00:26:48,900 --> 00:26:49,900
I'm not your playmate, Little Jam!

491
00:26:50,350 --> 00:26:51,190
Stop!

492
00:26:51,390 --> 00:26:51,990
Stop it!

493
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:53,040
Stop it already!

494
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:00,380
Stop.

495
00:27:00,600 --> 00:27:01,230
Stop it!

496
00:27:01,290 --> 00:27:02,320
Stop, stop.

497
00:27:02,380 --> 00:27:03,720
Stop, stop, stop...

498
00:27:04,650 --> 00:27:05,750
I told you to stop!

499
00:27:05,770 --> 00:27:06,440
Little Jam!

500
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:33,820
Little Jam.

501
00:27:35,230 --> 00:27:36,230
We're here.

502
00:27:37,340 --> 00:27:38,920
Already?

503
00:27:40,630 --> 00:27:41,730
Thank you.

504
00:27:48,330 --> 00:27:49,330
Come on.

505
00:27:55,930 --> 00:27:56,830
Don't rub your eyes.

506
00:27:58,630 --> 00:27:59,630
Or else they'll turn red.

507
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:01,250
Right.

508
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:04,230
Thank you for driving me here.

509
00:28:06,380 --> 00:28:07,940
Would you like to come inside first?

510
00:28:11,030 --> 00:28:11,940
Sure.

511
00:28:12,930 --> 00:28:13,930
And what about your parents?

512
00:28:20,260 --> 00:28:21,820
Mom and Dad

513
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:23,290
are in here.

514
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:34,330
I have been living alone since high school.

515
00:28:42,530 --> 00:28:43,530
Let us head inside, shall we?

516
00:28:43,670 --> 00:28:44,950
- Alright.
- Right.

517
00:29:18,540 --> 00:29:19,640
What's this?

518
00:29:21,230 --> 00:29:22,920
It is similar to a yogurt drink.

519
00:29:23,670 --> 00:29:25,670
I mixed it with soda just for you,

520
00:29:25,690 --> 00:29:26,940
so that it is easier to drink.

521
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:28,920
Feed me.

522
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:35,420
Would you like to drink it nicely,

523
00:29:35,750 --> 00:29:37,550
or shall I force-feed you?

524
00:29:38,340 --> 00:29:39,210
Whoa.

525
00:29:39,270 --> 00:29:40,320
No chill, huh?

526
00:29:46,150 --> 00:29:47,150
It's good, really.

527
00:29:54,820 --> 00:29:56,120
Your house is very lovely, you know?

528
00:30:02,340 --> 00:30:04,020
Can I take a look upstairs?

529
00:30:12,530 --> 00:30:13,340
Sure.

530
00:30:50,260 --> 00:30:51,710
Would you like a drink?

531
00:30:53,830 --> 00:30:55,450
Your cat's not home?

532
00:30:57,530 --> 00:30:58,920
You remember

533
00:30:58,940 --> 00:30:59,940
that I have a cat?

534
00:31:10,550 --> 00:31:11,440
I remember it all.

535
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:18,740
I left my cat with Ung-Ing.

536
00:31:19,250 --> 00:31:22,630
But I may have to have her
send it back to the cat hotel again.

537
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:27,740
Bring it with you to Pak Chong, then.

538
00:31:28,320 --> 00:31:29,540
I would rather not do that.

539
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:33,030
What would I do
if my cat grew to love the farm?

540
00:31:35,250 --> 00:31:36,430
Stay there forever, then.

541
00:31:42,030 --> 00:31:43,420
I would rather not.

542
00:31:44,310 --> 00:31:45,500
My cat

543
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:46,830
has to stay with me.

544
00:31:49,740 --> 00:31:51,340
Why don't you both stay there?

545
00:32:02,350 --> 00:32:04,240
Whoa! A crocodile...

546
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:14,820
This is Mr. Croc,
my beloved crocodile plush.

547
00:32:19,230 --> 00:32:20,740
I love him so much.

548
00:32:22,330 --> 00:32:24,800
Can I bring Mr. Croc to Pak Chong with me?

549
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:39,240
Are you hungry?

550
00:32:40,630 --> 00:32:43,310
My stomach has been growling
as if it is singing a cappella.

551
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:51,560
- Boo!
- Whoa!

552
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:54,920
Gosh, what are you doing, Little Jam?

553
00:32:55,950 --> 00:32:56,950
It is just Mr. Croc.

554
00:32:57,030 --> 00:32:58,030
This isn't fun.

555
00:32:58,220 --> 00:32:59,340
- Boo!
- Hey...

556
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:00,560
Boo!

557
00:33:02,350 --> 00:33:03,840
Boo!

558
00:33:06,540 --> 00:33:07,540
Boo!

559
00:33:23,190 --> 00:33:23,960
Hello?

560
00:33:24,930 --> 00:33:25,910
Yes, Ning-nong?

561
00:33:26,500 --> 00:33:27,250
Oh, I'm free.

562
00:33:28,380 --> 00:33:29,330
What is it?

563
00:33:30,460 --> 00:33:31,520
Tomorrow?

564
00:33:32,340 --> 00:33:33,530
Oh... Okay.

565
00:33:33,930 --> 00:33:34,930
What time?

566
00:33:36,830 --> 00:33:39,840
He is so nice when he talks to others,

567
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:41,430
but with me,

568
00:33:41,550 --> 00:33:43,020
he is always threatening me

569
00:33:43,090 --> 00:33:44,800
and getting on my nerves.

570
00:33:48,650 --> 00:33:49,360
Okay.

571
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:50,430
That said,

572
00:33:50,740 --> 00:33:51,670
Ning-nong,

573
00:33:51,690 --> 00:33:53,200
call me once you've clocked out.

574
00:33:54,340 --> 00:33:55,620
No, it's okay.

575
00:33:55,980 --> 00:33:56,560
Sure.

576
00:33:56,650 --> 00:33:57,510
Okay, then.

577
00:34:04,550 --> 00:34:05,730
Oh, it was Ning-nong.

578
00:34:06,290 --> 00:34:07,290
He's...

579
00:34:07,340 --> 00:34:08,670
a vet working at the stable,

580
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:11,310
and he's still new to Adisuan Farm.

581
00:34:11,949 --> 00:34:12,949
Tomorrow, he has to...

582
00:34:13,730 --> 00:34:15,230
go into town,
but he doesn't want to go there alone.

583
00:34:15,770 --> 00:34:16,929
So he asked me to accompany him.

584
00:34:17,719 --> 00:34:18,719
Join me, will you?

585
00:34:21,020 --> 00:34:22,020
I will pass.

586
00:34:22,580 --> 00:34:25,469
Tomorrow, I have to go to
the reservoir with Wasin.

587
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:34,750
No touching.

588
00:34:36,429 --> 00:34:37,320
No touching.

589
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,230
Come on.

590
00:34:38,320 --> 00:34:39,170
Look at you.

591
00:34:39,590 --> 00:34:40,719
Give me a hand massage, then.

592
00:34:43,670 --> 00:34:44,670
It was such a long drive here.

593
00:34:44,730 --> 00:34:45,880
My hands are killing me.

594
00:34:45,949 --> 00:34:46,949
A hand massage, please?

595
00:35:02,530 --> 00:35:03,450
Is it good?

596
00:35:03,470 --> 00:35:04,330
Uh-huh.

597
00:35:05,180 --> 00:35:06,370
And...

598
00:35:09,670 --> 00:35:11,720
When will you promote me
to be your number one,

599
00:35:13,030 --> 00:35:13,520
hm?

600
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:19,820
We will talk about it later
when you are hot enough.

601
00:35:19,840 --> 00:35:20,510
Ouch!

602
00:35:20,530 --> 00:35:21,440
Gosh, Jam.

603
00:35:21,570 --> 00:35:22,510
You and your words.

604
00:35:22,740 --> 00:35:23,640
Sure.

605
00:35:24,030 --> 00:35:25,030
If that's the case,

606
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:26,440
then I'll

607
00:35:26,460 --> 00:35:28,110
get serious about my training.

608
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:29,630
Training with who?

609
00:35:37,230 --> 00:35:37,960
Solo training.

610
00:35:38,570 --> 00:35:39,830
You are one massive pervert.

611
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,190
Whoa...

612
00:35:41,220 --> 00:35:42,450
Listen to you!

613
00:35:42,590 --> 00:35:44,230
Is this how you talk to a senior?

614
00:35:44,250 --> 00:35:45,550
Well, look at what you are doing.

615
00:35:50,180 --> 00:35:51,230
This will help you grow up fast.

616
00:35:56,230 --> 00:35:56,940
Is it good?

617
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:02,030
See?

618
00:36:02,120 --> 00:36:02,790
I told you so.

619
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:04,250
It's all your favorites.

620
00:36:05,950 --> 00:36:06,950
Boo!

621
00:36:08,430 --> 00:36:10,630
I do not even like crab the best.

622
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:13,020
You are just assuming things.

623
00:36:15,190 --> 00:36:16,840
You don't like eating crab?

624
00:36:17,340 --> 00:36:18,340
Then, you like...

625
00:36:24,980 --> 00:36:25,980
You like...

626
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:28,030
You like me, Little Jam?

627
00:36:28,550 --> 00:36:29,610
You like me...

628
00:36:30,210 --> 00:36:31,440
You don't like crab,

629
00:36:31,670 --> 00:36:32,420
but you like me.

630
00:36:32,510 --> 00:36:33,510
Are you hitting on me?

631
00:36:33,910 --> 00:36:35,040
Yes, just now realizing that?

632
00:36:41,430 --> 00:36:42,240
Oops...

633
00:36:43,490 --> 00:36:44,490
Yes, with a courting dance.

634
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:45,940
It goes like this.

635
00:36:46,300 --> 00:36:47,220
Like this.

636
00:36:58,500 --> 00:37:01,390
How did I forget what Mr. Sarm is like?

637
00:37:27,690 --> 00:37:34,110
[Salary Payment Records]

638
00:37:42,250 --> 00:37:43,320
I've got work to clear,

639
00:37:47,030 --> 00:37:48,430
life stuff to sort out,

640
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:53,530
and matters of the heart to handle.

641
00:37:59,510 --> 00:38:00,420
Mr. Sarm!

642
00:38:00,730 --> 00:38:02,210
It's only you, Little Jam,

643
00:38:02,230 --> 00:38:03,590
who are irresistibly adorable.

644
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:04,720
So cute.

645
00:38:04,740 --> 00:38:05,620
Smooch.

646
00:38:08,340 --> 00:38:09,620
You're the cutest.

647
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,010
Mr. Sarm!

648
00:38:13,030 --> 00:38:14,330
We've got a major problem!

649
00:38:14,490 --> 00:38:15,940
Lin-chee just called
and told me that Mr. Song

650
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:17,050
slipped and fell in the bathroom!

651
00:38:17,130 --> 00:38:17,800
Huh?!

652
00:38:21,230 --> 00:38:22,130
Mr. Song!

653
00:38:22,720 --> 00:38:24,030
- Oh, Mr. Sarm!
- Song!

654
00:38:25,020 --> 00:38:25,590
Aunt Salee,

655
00:38:25,660 --> 00:38:26,990
call an ambulance right away.

656
00:38:27,040 --> 00:38:27,800
Aunt Lin-chee,

657
00:38:27,820 --> 00:38:28,770
call the medical center!

658
00:38:28,790 --> 00:38:29,480
Right away!

659
00:38:35,860 --> 00:38:37,720
Whoa! What's going on?!

660
00:38:37,970 --> 00:38:38,620
Hey...

661
00:38:38,990 --> 00:38:40,430
What the hell are you doing here?!

662
00:38:40,530 --> 00:38:41,240
Song...

663
00:38:41,260 --> 00:38:42,330
What are you all doing here?

664
00:38:42,350 --> 00:38:42,820
What?

665
00:38:42,940 --> 00:38:44,150
She said you fell!

666
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:45,700
Earlier,

667
00:38:45,810 --> 00:38:47,510
I heard you screaming,

668
00:38:47,540 --> 00:38:48,910
followed by loud noises.

669
00:38:48,950 --> 00:38:51,020
I kept knocking on the door,
but you wouldn't open it.

670
00:38:51,040 --> 00:38:52,710
You didn't respond either.

671
00:38:52,770 --> 00:38:55,920
I panicked and called Salee...

672
00:38:59,090 --> 00:39:00,120
So did you fall or not?

673
00:39:01,930 --> 00:39:03,230
I actually did,

674
00:39:03,500 --> 00:39:05,320
but I'm fine.

675
00:39:06,020 --> 00:39:07,240
If you weren't hurt,

676
00:39:07,260 --> 00:39:08,800
why didn't you respond?

677
00:39:11,040 --> 00:39:11,910
I didn't hear her!

678
00:39:12,670 --> 00:39:13,320
Oh...

679
00:39:15,870 --> 00:39:16,570
You two,

680
00:39:17,010 --> 00:39:18,830
you may go and have a rest now.

681
00:39:19,030 --> 00:39:20,030
Also,

682
00:39:20,240 --> 00:39:21,490
call and inform

683
00:39:21,630 --> 00:39:23,050
those at the main house.

684
00:39:23,220 --> 00:39:24,220
Understood, Mr. Sarm.

685
00:39:24,350 --> 00:39:25,530
Understood.

686
00:39:29,030 --> 00:39:30,410
Always causing trouble.

687
00:39:30,830 --> 00:39:32,040
How would I know?

688
00:39:32,780 --> 00:39:34,140
Always clueless.

689
00:39:48,470 --> 00:39:49,840
What the hell did you do

690
00:39:50,130 --> 00:39:50,840
to fall like that?

691
00:39:51,690 --> 00:39:52,690
I was doing a dance cover.

692
00:40:00,130 --> 00:40:01,230
I slipped on some soap.

693
00:40:03,470 --> 00:40:04,230
Right.

694
00:40:04,670 --> 00:40:05,810
Now, it's your turn.

695
00:40:06,700 --> 00:40:07,930
I've been meaning to ask you this.

696
00:40:09,730 --> 00:40:11,630
You don't seem like a heartbroken person.

697
00:40:12,530 --> 00:40:14,430
More than anything,
you seem like you're in love.

698
00:40:17,310 --> 00:40:18,020
Is something going on?

699
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:18,720
Really?

700
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:22,800
Okay.

701
00:40:27,570 --> 00:40:28,520
Actually,

702
00:40:28,890 --> 00:40:29,710
you know...

703
00:40:31,120 --> 00:40:32,320
I thought I'd never

704
00:40:32,340 --> 00:40:34,740
feel this way
about anyone again in my life...

705
00:40:39,630 --> 00:40:41,330
but this kid is the exception.

706
00:40:43,940 --> 00:40:45,520
Whenever I'm with this one,

707
00:40:46,470 --> 00:40:47,820
I'm over the moon.

708
00:40:49,050 --> 00:40:50,320
I feel really comfortable.

709
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:54,320
I want us to be together

710
00:40:54,530 --> 00:40:55,340
all the time.

711
00:40:59,130 --> 00:41:00,400
Talking about it makes me miss this kid.

712
00:41:01,730 --> 00:41:03,120
From the looks of it,

713
00:41:03,530 --> 00:41:04,990
you're head over heels.

714
00:41:06,730 --> 00:41:07,400
Nonsense...

715
00:41:07,420 --> 00:41:08,290
By the way,

716
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:11,790
who is this person?

717
00:41:11,810 --> 00:41:12,520
I'm not telling.

718
00:41:12,540 --> 00:41:14,150
Hey, why are you hiding it from me?

719
00:41:14,230 --> 00:41:15,420
It's not the right time yet.

720
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:16,040
Come on...

721
00:41:16,060 --> 00:41:16,840
Here's the deal.

722
00:41:17,130 --> 00:41:18,540
I don't want to keep this a secret,

723
00:41:19,620 --> 00:41:21,630
but when this person says yes,

724
00:41:22,180 --> 00:41:23,710
I swear

725
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,480
I'll put up announcements on billboards

726
00:41:25,730 --> 00:41:27,320
in all four directions of our farm.

727
00:41:27,340 --> 00:41:29,430
I'll make an announcement
after breakfast, lunch, and dinner every day

728
00:41:29,450 --> 00:41:30,670
for all seven days.

729
00:41:31,130 --> 00:41:32,730
That's more like it, Sarm.

730
00:41:35,100 --> 00:41:36,340
You're crazy.

731
00:41:36,650 --> 00:41:38,130
Waiting for the kid to say yes?

732
00:41:38,220 --> 00:41:39,830
Have you made a move yet?

733
00:41:39,850 --> 00:41:41,430
Have you made it clear?

734
00:41:42,290 --> 00:41:43,860
Have you made a move yet, Sarm?

735
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:44,620
Answer me.

736
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:46,550
I haven't.

737
00:41:47,220 --> 00:41:48,430
I thought so.

738
00:41:48,450 --> 00:41:49,540
What seems to be the problem?

739
00:41:49,560 --> 00:41:51,820
Why didn't you tell the kid how you feel?

740
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:53,700
Today,

741
00:41:54,080 --> 00:41:55,340
the kid did actually ask me.

742
00:41:56,330 --> 00:41:58,230
So I just jokingly said that

743
00:41:58,490 --> 00:41:59,430
I was making a move.

744
00:42:00,280 --> 00:42:02,130
And the reaction I got
was nothing but shock.

745
00:42:03,050 --> 00:42:04,310
I didn't know what to do next,

746
00:42:04,820 --> 00:42:06,010
so I just kept joking around.

747
00:42:07,780 --> 00:42:09,220
Take this seriously, Sarm.

748
00:42:09,340 --> 00:42:10,140
In this story,

749
00:42:10,170 --> 00:42:11,470
you're the main character, alright?

750
00:42:16,030 --> 00:42:16,710
I know.

751
00:42:18,050 --> 00:42:19,290
I've got one last question

752
00:42:19,310 --> 00:42:20,840
for you tonight.

753
00:42:20,870 --> 00:42:21,580
Right.

754
00:42:22,330 --> 00:42:23,560
What did this person do

755
00:42:23,580 --> 00:42:24,740
to make you

756
00:42:24,760 --> 00:42:26,640
fall head over heels?

757
00:42:29,070 --> 00:42:30,350
For this question,

758
00:42:30,830 --> 00:42:31,830
let me just say this.

759
00:42:32,290 --> 00:42:33,240
This kid

760
00:42:33,260 --> 00:42:34,320
didn't have to do anything.

761
00:42:34,830 --> 00:42:36,210
Just sitting there doing nothing

762
00:42:37,330 --> 00:42:39,140
already makes me want to
sign this house away.

763
00:42:39,830 --> 00:42:40,390
That much?

764
00:42:40,410 --> 00:42:41,100
Yeah.

765
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:43,430
Everywhere I go, I see this kid's face.

766
00:42:44,450 --> 00:42:45,630
You've fallen hard, haven't you?

767
00:42:47,310 --> 00:42:48,440
You're really asking for it, aren't you?

768
00:42:48,460 --> 00:42:50,120
Sarm, get off me!

769
00:42:50,270 --> 00:42:52,260
Get the hell away from me, Sarm!

770
00:42:52,280 --> 00:42:53,140
You dare kick me?

771
00:42:53,160 --> 00:42:55,210
I'll kick you again if you don't stop.

772
00:42:55,710 --> 00:42:56,670
Sarm!

773
00:42:57,610 --> 00:42:59,190
You can't do anything to me.

774
00:43:00,670 --> 00:43:02,520
Why are you trying to kiss me on the cheek?!

775
00:43:02,540 --> 00:43:04,260
Because you're cute today.

776
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:05,030
Stop!

777
00:43:05,050 --> 00:43:06,750
Today, you're done for!

778
00:43:09,750 --> 00:43:10,750
Gosh.

779
00:43:11,430 --> 00:43:12,620
Since returning from the island,

780
00:43:12,650 --> 00:43:14,730
not a single day has gone by
without some problem.

781
00:43:14,840 --> 00:43:16,830
Work keeps slipping through the cracks daily.

782
00:43:18,630 --> 00:43:19,550
Thee.

783
00:43:19,770 --> 00:43:20,670
You little instigator.

784
00:43:20,690 --> 00:43:21,620
You got rid of your own people,

785
00:43:21,650 --> 00:43:22,850
brought outsiders in,

786
00:43:22,870 --> 00:43:24,360
and rigged the system to fail.

787
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:27,630
And all departments
are constantly fighting with each other.

788
00:43:28,080 --> 00:43:29,940
Despite knowing what he's been doing,

789
00:43:30,100 --> 00:43:31,690
I somehow

790
00:43:31,710 --> 00:43:32,740
remain calm.

791
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:35,120
I'm mentally exhausted,

792
00:43:35,330 --> 00:43:36,740
but I can't blame anyone else,

793
00:43:37,180 --> 00:43:38,320
as I brought this on myself.

794
00:43:39,090 --> 00:43:40,340
Work is important,

795
00:43:40,940 --> 00:43:42,540
and so are matters of my heart.

796
00:43:43,130 --> 00:43:44,130
At first...

797
00:43:45,180 --> 00:43:47,550
I was struck by his heart-stopping cuteness.

798
00:43:48,080 --> 00:43:48,950
And then...

799
00:43:49,560 --> 00:43:51,130
it left a lasting impression.

800
00:43:51,530 --> 00:43:54,140
We went through so much and developed a bond.

801
00:43:54,650 --> 00:43:55,640
By the time I realized it,

802
00:43:56,240 --> 00:43:57,920
Little Jam had popped up out of nowhere

803
00:43:58,190 --> 00:44:00,740
and cutely nestled his way into my heart.

804
00:44:06,390 --> 00:44:07,210
"Little Jam...

805
00:44:09,830 --> 00:44:11,040
I like you."

806
00:44:12,190 --> 00:44:13,240
Too direct?

807
00:44:13,500 --> 00:44:14,610
No, no, no.

808
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:18,230
"Little Jam.

809
00:44:19,530 --> 00:44:21,100
This man from Pak Chong

810
00:44:21,660 --> 00:44:23,240
is in it for the long haul."

811
00:44:24,040 --> 00:44:24,730
Nuts.

812
00:44:25,220 --> 00:44:26,340
If I actually said that,

813
00:44:26,730 --> 00:44:28,040
he'd tease me about it until I'm old.

814
00:44:29,220 --> 00:44:30,220
What should I say?

815
00:44:31,390 --> 00:44:32,030
"Freeze!

816
00:44:33,160 --> 00:44:34,330
This is a robbery.

817
00:44:36,130 --> 00:44:38,720
Hand over the title of
your number one spouse to me.

818
00:44:38,770 --> 00:44:40,050
Or else,

819
00:44:41,730 --> 00:44:43,350
I'll kiss your cheeks until they deflate!"

820
00:44:48,940 --> 00:44:50,330
If I confessed my feelings

821
00:44:50,830 --> 00:44:52,440
and he didn't feel the same,

822
00:44:52,590 --> 00:44:53,530
what would I do?

823
00:44:59,390 --> 00:45:01,050
"It's fine if you don't feel the same.

824
00:45:03,530 --> 00:45:05,020
Just seeing you happy

825
00:45:05,330 --> 00:45:06,440
with someone you like

826
00:45:09,340 --> 00:45:10,420
makes me happy, too."

827
00:45:14,630 --> 00:45:15,740
Just kidding!

828
00:45:15,960 --> 00:45:16,730
Come on, Little Jam!

829
00:45:16,780 --> 00:45:17,780
I like you!

830
00:45:17,800 --> 00:45:19,180
I can't take it anymore!

831
00:45:19,210 --> 00:45:20,990
Little Jam!

832
00:45:22,000 --> 00:45:22,940
Let's go.

833
00:45:29,080 --> 00:45:29,970
Hey, Jam!

834
00:45:29,990 --> 00:45:30,740
Be careful!

835
00:45:31,680 --> 00:45:33,930
We need to take him
to the medical center, Mr. Thee.

836
00:45:33,960 --> 00:45:35,900
You're new here,
so I guess you don't know who I am.

837
00:45:36,540 --> 00:45:38,850
There is still a lot more
that I need to learn.

838
00:45:38,890 --> 00:45:40,530
Please take care of me and guide me.

839
00:45:41,030 --> 00:45:42,150
You can call me by my name.

840
00:45:42,170 --> 00:45:43,010
Mr. Sarm!

841
00:45:43,030 --> 00:45:43,940
How did you get here?

842
00:45:45,480 --> 00:45:46,930
Your limbs are all hurt.

843
00:45:46,950 --> 00:45:48,280
How can you go back to living alone?

844
00:45:51,620 --> 00:45:52,820
Mr. Sarm.

845
00:45:59,030 --> 00:46:05,220
♫It seems like something's moving♫

846
00:46:05,300 --> 00:46:11,740
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

847
00:46:11,770 --> 00:46:15,960
♫I only wish you nothing but the best♫

848
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:20,310
♫Hoping your smile will never fade♫

849
00:46:20,340 --> 00:46:25,130
♫That's all, for I don't wish
to take someone's place♫

850
00:46:25,190 --> 00:46:29,390
♫I'll simply be right here, always within reach♫

851
00:46:29,440 --> 00:46:33,890
♫Like a gentle breeze bringing you peace♫

852
00:46:33,950 --> 00:46:40,520
